  "title": "Loop Engineering: The Guy Who Built Claude Code Says He Doesn't Prompt Anymore",
  "description": "The biggest shift in AI isn't better prompting. It's building systems that keep working after you stop typing.\n\nLoop engineering turns Claude Code from a chatbot into an autonomous workflow by combining automations, worktrees, skills, connectors, and sub-agents into a self-improving loop.\n\nInstead of constantly prompting the AI, you give it a goal. It plans, executes, reviews its own work, remembers progress, and keeps going until the task is complete.\n\nThis is how the best AI engineers are getting dramatically more done with the same models.\n\n#claudecode #aiagents #automation #coding #developer #ai",
  "publishedAt": "2026-06-28T18:10:02Z",
  "channel_name": "AI adventurer",
  "transcript": "The biggest shift in AI isn't better prompting. It's building systems that keep working after you stop typing.\n\nLoop engineering turns Claude Code from a chatbot into an autonomous workflow by combining automations, worktrees, skills, connectors, and sub-agents into a self-improving loop.\n\nInstead of constantly prompting the AI, you give it a goal. It plans, executes, reviews its own work, remembers progress, and keeps going until the task is complete.\n\nThis is how the best AI engineers are getting dramatically more done with the same models.\n\n#claudecode #aiagents #automation #coding #developer #ai",
